1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Josephine Angelica Bidoulac (11/05/1812 to 12/02/1866), daughter of French immigrants to Denmark: language teacher Joseph Bidoulac, Denmark (1765-1839) and Mumche Marie Sørensen (1783-1850). 
2 CONT
2 CONT "a lively and clever girl"
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Johan Sebastian Welhaven 05/27/1845. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Josephine Angelica Bidoulac.: Her father, Joseph Bidoulac, was a French emigrant who had settled in Denmark, where he married Mumche Marie Sorensen, and where his daughter was born in Flensburg, Nov. 5. The 1812th In the midst of 
2 CONC 30th year she came as private tutor to Drøbak when she was about three years and from which she often came for a visit to Professor Hansteen of Christiania; here was Welhaven acquainted with her, and he was with Joseph Bidoulac an
2 CONC d Mumche Marie Sorensen.
