1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Stanford University Alumni Ex-'O1—Mrs. Alfred Welhaven (Emilie Stevenson) has lived in Korea for the last ten years. Mr. Welhaven is general manager of the Oriental Consolidated Mining Company, Unsau, Korea. They h
2 CONC ave two daughters, Karen and Elisabeth. Border Crossings From Canada to United States, 1895-1956 for Emelie Welhaven
2 CONT
2 CONT "Concerned about diseases, vegetables sold at the Korean markets were avoided by many of the Westerners living in Korea because they were fertilized with human fecal matter. This led to a somewhat awkward moment when a group of vo
2 CONC lunteers for the Red Cross visited the OCMC mines to put on a show for the miners following World War One. When they sat down to eat, the mine manager’s wife, Mrs. Welhaven, noted one of her guests was reluctant to eat the fresh v
2 CONC egetables. She clumsily tried to reassure her guest that the vegetables were safe to eat. “Don’t be afraid to eat, my dear, these are grown in our own manure.”25 Embarrassed laughter greeted the blushing and flustered hostess, but
2 CONC  all understood her meaning." http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:Nhvdr1LI884J:raskb.inje.ac.kr/main/original_download2.php%3Ffilepath%3DD:%255CAPM_Setup%255Chtdocs%255CContents/2011/11/14/764C32AD-9F29-44EB-8E00-
