2 DATE 30 DEC 2004
2 ADDR
3 CITY Portland
3 STAE OR
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Dec. 16, 1917 Portland Multnomah County Oregon, USA Death: 	Dec. 30, 2004
2 CONT
2 CONT "Betty" was born to DeWitt "Tal" Talmadge and Daphne Holloway Hillis. Betty spent her childhood in Brownsville and Portland. She graduated from Franklin High School..."Maroon & Gray! Fight! Fight!"
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1938, she married Eric Dean Anderson. Dean died in 1994, just short of their 56th anniversary. Betty worked for several years at Fred Meyer and served as a Red Cross Gray Lady during World War II. Betty is survived by son, Mark
2 CONC , and his wife, Beverly Anderson, Bay City; daughter, Gail E. Anderson, Portland; grandchildren, Leslie E. Anderson, Wilsonville and Chris Eric Anderson, Portland; great-grandchild, Clarence Dean Anderson, Garibaldi; niece, Diane 
2 CONC Carlsen, and her husband, Loren, Portland; and nephew, David Hillis, and his wife, Rita, West Linn. Betty's beloved brother, Bob, and "sister", Bert Hillis, preceded her in death. The family expresses their sincere thanks to Betty
2 CONC 's devoted caregivers, the loving Lily Bobu and family, and the "beautiful" Ronela Muntean. Their tender care made her life so comfortable. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Published in The Oregonian on 1/13/2005. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Lone Fir Pioneer Cemetery  Portland Multnomah County Oregon, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Sheri West Record added: Feb 07, 2005  Find A Grave Memorial# 10442267
