1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hanna Charlotte graduated from dental school (unusual for a woman to be a university graduate in WWI) but never practiced dentistry as a profession.  While she was living on her husband's ship, she did dental work 
2 CONC for some of the Chinese crew, who were very grateful to her.  When she lived at Fjellveien 1 in Lysaker (from 1933), she had a dental chair in the attic. During WWII, she worked on her kids' teeth at home. They were a lot less gra
2 CONC teful.
